		{
			"id": "eS_GN5vZgY0W8ge2q",
			"description": "Plasma Gun",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The plasma gun is the Guard's and the Astartes' standard answer to power armour and light vehicles alike; fiction from Gaunt's Ghosts to Space Marine Battles depicts it killing power-armoured targets outright while carrying a real chance of cooking its own wielder, especially on older, less stable patterns - the origin of the tabletop and RPG \"gets hot\"/ overheat mechanic this entry represents mechanically as Malf 14 on the supercharged line.\n\nDesign: This is the project's fixed plasma anchor: 6dx2(3) burn ex, treated as the weapon's safe standard mode (no Malf risk) since it is already stated in the framework to kill Marines through power armour without needing to invoke overheating. Check: Astartes power armour is torso DR 40; armour divisor (3) drops effective DR to about 13.3, and 6dx2 averages 42, so it penetrates and kills reliably, as required. Against a Terminator's DR 80 (effective DR ~26.7) the average of 42 still gets through, matching the framework's explicit statement that plasma still kills Terminators. The supercharged mode (6dx3(3), Malf 14) exists for harder targets (light vehicles, multiple Terminators) at the cost of a real chance of the coil failing and burning the firer, matching the fiction's running theme of plasma weapons being feared by their own side almost as much as by the enemy.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "3200",
			"base_weight": "14 lb",
